# The function overwrites its saved lr with r0 = 0x4001 before pop {pc}. On the hardware it
# would branch there; a recompiled function returns with a C return, so it can only go back
# to its caller, and MT_CHECK_RETURNS stops it with MT_TRAP_BAD_RETURN at the pop (detail =
# the target). pop has already written sp back.
title: pop {pc} to an address other than the entry lr stops with MT_TRAP_BAD_RETURN at the pop
ref: A8.8 PUSH T1, STR (immediate, Thumb) T2, POP (Thumb) T1: LoadWritePC(); ADR 0014: returns are C returns, checked against the entry lr

[code]
00b5        push {lr}
0090        str r0, [sp]
00bd        pop {pc}

[in]
r0 = 0x4001

[out]
trap = bad_return BASE+4 0x4001
word SP0-4 = 0x4001
